{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"privileged-nephelite-colt","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A folded prior SNAPSHOT is not a lost event\n\n`fsck_repair.snapshot_missing_sources` flags any cited `source_event_uuids` entry with no\nfile on disk. But when compaction folds a ticket, the SUPERSEDED SNAPSHOT is itself listed as\na source of its successor, and that snapshot file is then legitimately gone — consumed. No\ndata is lost: a snapshot's entire content IS its `compiled_state`, which the successor\nabsorbed.\n\nTreating that as an incomplete log is wrong twice over: it reports a healthy ticket as\ndamaged, and (post b636) it makes the ticket look un-rebuildable.\n\n## Evidence\nAfter the b636 remediation, 6 tickets still report SNAPSHOT_MISSING_SOURCES:\n316c-6c42-32d3-4f9b, a6ea-6a28-1d84-4626, bbc0-1dbd-d9cb-4917, be08-b46d-51be-419d,\nc7c5-12ea-ad68-4690, e0d4-4f19-699d-4d61.\nEach is missing EXACTLY ONE uuid, and in every case that uuid resolves (via the path it was\nadded at in tickets history) to a `-SNAPSHOT.json` event. All six reduce to `closed`\ncorrectly — their state is intact. The 7th (f130) was a genuine EDIT loss and was repaired\nseparately.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `snapshot_missing_sources` does NOT count a cited uuid whose event is a SNAPSHOT\n      superseded by the citing snapshot. Determine the type without a history walk where\n      possible (the reducer/compaction knows which uuid was the folded snapshot).\n- [ ] The six tickets above report clean afterwards, with their status unchanged.\n- [ ] A genuinely missing raw event is still reported (no weakening of the b636 guard) —\n      held-out test asserts both directions.\n- [ ] Consider recording the folded snapshot uuid distinctly in the SNAPSHOT payload so the\n      distinction is structural rather than inferred.","id":"aea0-0dac-b501-464c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"SNAPSHOT_MISSING_SOURCES false-positives when the missing source is a consumed prior SNAPSHOT"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786296641505208001,"uuid":"adaca50e-61e2-40fa-b989-f6e308db22f8"}